        "Attributes": [
          {
            "Id": 758255,
            "attributeType": "LongString",
            "attributeName": "AIDescription",
            "attributeRelationType": "None",
            "Value": "The Atari 2600, originally launched in 1977 as the Atari Video Computer System (VCS), revolutionized home gaming. Developed by Atari, Inc., it popularized microprocessor-based hardware and the use of ROM cartridges, a format pioneered by the Fairchild Channel F. Bundled with joysticks and early hits like *Combat* and *Pac-Man*, the console quickly became a cultural phenomenon, with \"Atari\" becoming synonymous with video games. \n\nDriven by the desire for a programmable system, the Atari 2600 featured iconic titles like *Space Invaders*, *Adventure* (introducing the first Easter egg), and *Asteroids*, often utilizing bank switching to expand game capabilities. Despite its success, rushed releases like *Pac-Man* and *E.T.* contributed to the 1983 video game crash. Though production ended in 1992, the Atari 2600 remains a landmark console, inducted into the National Toy Hall of Fame and inspiring later generations of gaming."
          },
